          Greetings one and all!  Allow me to introduce myself.  I be Paladin Dragoons, better known in a former life as the notorious druid Droken Flirtsalot.  I cordially invite you all to a tournament of champions.  Come test thine martial skills, relax in the company of fellow champions in merry laughter and conversation, drink in toast to the festivities, and gaze in awe as warriors from afar battle it out in duels to the death!  If bloodshed be not thine prefferable sport, then just come and be a spectator to the different fighting styles of the land.  This tournament primarilly invites and encourages warriors, rangers, shadowknights, monks, rogues and paladins to test their blades and courage amongst one another in honorable combat, but casters are just as welcome.  Lay hands will not be allowed, nor harm touch, to make things more fair in tank matches as we all know 'tis quite an overwhelming advantage compared to our non magic using brethren of the blade.  They will be allowed against spell casters, however, keep in mind you may only call upon these holy and unholy powers once per day, and in this tournament one loss disqualifies your chance at victory.  The restrictions will allow for those within the levels of 32-36.  I currently only stand at 29 myself, but will hopefully fall within this category before the start of the event next Friday.  Grand prize victor will be awarded 1000pp my yours truly, and anyone who falls within this level range may also personally challenge myself, and any win against me will win you a bonus 200pp.  The tournament will officially start at 6 pacific, Friday of next week.  This should allow time for everyone to get off work and relax a bit before the battle begins.  Arrive early and relax, not late.  6pm pacific is 9 eastern.  It will be held in the arena in Freeport, as I don't believe the Freeport guards come near this area.  Just have someone invis you in and make sure to get bound.  If on the off chance I am incorrect, we could just as easilly move over to Qeynos and if even that doesn't work the official Arena in lake rathe.  Leaving the arena grounds during battle grants automatic disqualification.  'Tis all in the name of pride and fun, and even a chance at free money.  No entry fee.  Practice up on your dueling before you arrive unprepared.  make sure to bring whatever necessities you might require, ie small daggers, melatite, cats eye agate, etc.  Be forwarned however, that my own personal dueling record currently stands at 18 wins, 0 losses, and also watch out for what I call the "Joust" maneuver.  Train well, and may I see you all next Friday evening!!<br>
          <br>
          Yours truly,<br>
          <br>
          Dragoons  <br>

